      "MAR row CM-42 S3 (F-CURR-002 section 9.2, 2026-10-30; passes: author, language, culture and facts, learning design, reviser, third pass). Volume 2 of Play & Crafts at Stage 3: rule sentences for taking turns (___ 차례예요), throwing (___ 던져요) and winning (___ 이겼어요), one new pattern a quest.",
      "Language: 해요체 with sentence marks; spacing 한 번 더, 우리 팀이; particle rounds test 을/를 and 이/가 (호야가, 팀이, 공을, 팽이를, 축구를); romanization by the converter (charyeyeyo, igyeosseoyo, uri timi, han beon deo). 다시 해요 is the polite suggestion, glossed Let's play again.",
      "Language (cont.): every word gap keeps grammatical wrong tiles (한 번 더 가요, 바다에 던져요, 다시 가요), so the gap is read by its meaning line, as in Volume 1; no tile is right for the meaning shown.",
      "Learning design: 내 and 네 sound alike (Word Builder q1), so 네 차례 is not taught and no heard round, Check or distractor holds 내 차례예요 against another spelling (F-CURR-001 section 3.5); 내 차례예요 is built and read only. Dictation asks 공 and 연 (one taught spelling each, said as written); 던져요 [던저요] and 차례예요 stay out of it.",
      "Learning design (cont.): 차례 is a homograph (turn; and the memorial rite 차례 of OD-9, not taught yet): it is taught only inside sentences, never as a bare word item, so the Holidays row that teaches the rite keeps its own item. 개 and 모 (throw names, also dog and seedling) appear only in note n2. New words: q1 내, 차례; q2 높이, 한 번, 더; q3 이겼어요, 우리, 팀, 다시.",
      "Learning design (cont.): triples q1 order-it / cloze-pick / order-it, q2 order-it / cloze-pick / type-hangul, q3 order-it / listen-pick / cloze-pick, none equal to a Volume 1 triple or its neighbour; three different produce Checks; every Practice is a Sentence Builder, so each can scaffold (CM-24). Practice and Check recycle 43, 57 and 43 in 100 (lesson-recycle); 3 new units a quest.",
      "Culture and facts: n1 (turns and winning) and n2 (the five throw names, 도 one and 모 five) each re-checked against the Standard Korean Language Dictionary and the Korea Heritage Service page for the National Intangible Heritage 윷놀이, named as of the access date; no UNESCO, designation or origin claim; no real person, shop, brand or price; no age wording.",
